      - demand_history_120d      kind=dataset            src=planner_node_2
        schema_hint: ['date', 'sku_id', 'warehouse', 'actual_consumption_qty', 'demand_including_lost_qty', 'market_index', 'planned_maintenance_flag', 'stockout_lost_qty', 'unit_replacement_price', 'source_channel']
      - market_signals           kind=dataset            src=planner_node_2
        schema_hint: ['week_start', 'category', 'region', 'demand_index', 'maintenance_cycle_index', 'customer_backlog_index', 'competitor_supply_shock', 'note']
      - supplier_performance     kind=dataset            src=planner_node_2
        schema_hint: ['supplier_id', 'supplier_name', 'region', 'contract_leadtime_days', 'latest_leadtime_days', 'on_time_rate', 'default_moq', 'quality_ppm', 'reliability_grade', 'last_delay_event']
  output.primary    : inventory_risk_assessment kind=dataset           
        schema_hint: ['sku_id', 'warehouse', 'risk_score', 'risk_category', 'days_until_stockout', 'recommended_reorder_qty', 'forecast_demand_30d', 'forecast_demand_60d', 'forecast_demand_90d', 'lead_time_risk', 'demand_volatility', 'criticality_score', 'analysis_timestamp']
  business_rules    : 5
      - [domain_policy] Risk score must be computed as a weighted combination of days until stockout, demand volatility, lead time reliability, and criticality. Weights: stockout_days 0.3, demand_volatility 0.25, lead_time_risk 0.25, criticality 0.2.
      - [value_mapping] Risk category mapping: risk_score >= 0.7 -> 'High', 0.4 <= risk_score < 0.7 -> 'Medium', risk_score < 0.4 -> 'Low'.
      - [domain_policy] Forecast demand for 30/60/90 days must use a time-series method (e.g., exponential smoothing or moving average) on actual_consumption_qty from demand_history_120d, adjusted by market_index and planned_maintenance_flag.
  acceptance        : 6
      - [row_count] Output dataset must contain exactly one row per (sku_id, warehouse) combination present in inventory_rt.
      - [value_range] risk_score must be a float between 0 and 1 inclusive.
      - [enum_membership] risk_category must be one of 'High', 'Medium', 'Low'.
  sketch            : 6 bullets
      • Load all five input datasets (sku_master, inventory_rt, demand_history_120d, market_signals, supplier_performance) from upstream node output.
      • Merge datasets on sku_id and warehouse to create a unified analysis record per SKU-warehouse pair.
      • Compute average daily consumption from last 30 days of demand_history_120d, adjusting for market_index and planned maintenance flags.
      • Calculate days until stockout using available_qty and average daily consumption; compute demand volatility as coefficient of variation of daily consumption.
      • Derive lead time risk from supplier_performance fields; compute weighted risk score and assign risk category.
      • Generate forecast demand for 30/60/90 days using exponential smoothing on historical consumption; output final risk assessment dataset with all required fields.

== planner_node_4  (runtime_class=bounded_transform) ==
  semantic_goal     : Forecast future demand using historical consumption and market demand signals
  inputs.required   : 3
      - demand_history_120d      kind=csv                src=planner_node_2
        schema_hint: ['date', 'sku_id', 'warehouse', 'actual_consumption_qty', 'demand_including_lost_qty', 'market_index', 'planned_maintenance_flag', 'stockout_lost_qty', 'unit_replacement_price', 'source_channel']
      - market_signals           kind=csv                src=planner_node_2
        schema_hint: ['week_start', 'category', 'region', 'demand_index', 'maintenance_cycle_index', 'customer_backlog_index', 'competitor_supply_shock', 'note']
      - sku_master               kind=csv                src=planner_node_2
        schema_hint: ['sku_id', 'part_name', 'category', 'criticality', 'unit', 'unit_cost', 'supplier_id', 'lead_time_days', 'moq', 'reorder_multiple', 'target_service_level', 'shelf_life_days', 'lifecycle', 'substitution_group', 'max_stock', 'base_daily_demand']
  output.primary    : demand_forecast          kind=csv               
        schema_hint: ['sku_id', 'warehouse', 'forecast_date', 'forecast_qty', 'forecast_upper_bound', 'forecast_lower_bound', 'confidence_level', 'method_used']
  business_rules    : 4
      - [completeness] Forecast must be generated per (sku_id, warehouse) pair using at least 30 days of historical data; if less than 30 days available, use base_daily_demand from sku_master as fallback.
      - [value_mapping] Market demand_index and maintenance_cycle_index from market_signals must be applied as multiplicative factors to the baseline forecast for the corresponding category and region.
      - [domain_policy] Forecast horizon must be 30 days from the current date (latest date in demand_history_120d).
  acceptance        : 5
      - [row_count] Output contains exactly one row per (sku_id, warehouse) per forecast day for the 30-day horizon.
      - [value_range] All forecast_qty values are non-negative.
      - [relational_integrity] Every sku_id in the output exists in the sku_master input.
  sketch            : 6 bullets
      • Load the three input datasets (demand_history_120d, market_signals, sku_master) from the upstream node's output.
      • For each (sku_id, warehouse) pair, compute a baseline daily forecast using time-series decomposition (e.g., moving average or exponential smoothing) on actual_consumption_qty; if insufficient history, fall back to base_daily_demand from sku_master.
      • Join with market_signals on category and region to apply demand_index and maintenance_cycle_index as multiplicative adjustments per week.
      • Generate a 30-day forecast table with upper/lower bounds based on historical variability (e.g., standard deviation of forecast errors).
      • Handle lifecycle-based exceptions: set forecast to 0 for discontinued/phase-out SKUs.
      • Write the output CSV with columns: sku_id, warehouse, forecast_date, forecast_qty, forecast_upper_bound, forecast_lower_bound, confidence_level, method_used.

